[21:57:58] 💭 The problem: the Makefile includes `/common.env` (absolute path at filesystem root) which doesn't exist in this container, and `Makefile.env` includes `$(ROOTDIR)/common.env` where `ROOTDIR` is derived from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` — which fails because git is masked (hideGit=true), so ROOTDIR is empty → `$(ROOTDIR)/common.env` becomes `/common.env`, and `make` reports "No rule to make target '/common.env'".

There IS a `/workspace/common.env` file (159 bytes). The Makefile was designed t…
[21:57:59] The failure is environmental: `ROOTDIR` is derived from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (Makefile.variables:3), which fails under hideGit's masked `.git`, leaving `$(ROOTDIR)/common.env` as `/common.env` — but `/workspace/common.env` exists. Since `ROOTDIR` uses `?=`, I can supply it explicitly. Let me check the remaining included files for other git dependencies first.


[21:57:59] $ cat /workspace/Makefile.variables /workspace/Makefile.docker /workspace/Makefile.env; echo "===common.env==="; cat /workspace/common.env; echo "===tools.env==="; cat /workspace/tools.env 2>/dev/null …
